# What the reports show

Ticket #4471 combines reports that the knowledge base classifies as two different problems. The shared parser read dates month-first for day-first tenants. Booking v3 also showed a month-first hint even though its form read dates in the tenant's format.

## Engineering update

The desk closed #4471 on 5 October. The parser was fixed in `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. The hint will not be fixed because booking v3 was retired. The two issues have different outcomes: completed for the parser, not planned for the hint.

The table uses unique report IDs, tenant locales, form versions and channels. Intake tags are guesses based on the browser and do not determine the cause. Its counts are recomputed from the export when the page renders.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Five reports in the desk notes describe a possible one-day move. The current classifier counts them under the parser based on tenant and channel; investigate their details before concluding they share that defect. The export is a snapshot, so check the live desk before treating its counts as current.

## When reports arrived and were merged

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

The desk's accepted subject-only deduplication rule can merge different causes and split reports of the same cause. Use tenant, channel and report details when triaging; do not amend the accepted decision record. Record any replacement decision separately.

